sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch09-04> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Wholly soft-bodied organisms are not preserved as fossils, and shells and bones decay and disappear where they lie on parts of the sea floor where sediment is not accumulating, so the fossil record is strongly biased.";
    dc:type "empirical-generalization";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Soft-bodied organisms and remains on non-depositing sea floor are not preserved";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Charles Darwin, On the Origin of Species (1st ed., London: John Murray, 1859), Chapter IX, “On the Imperfection of the Geological Record”; section “On the poorness of our palæontological collections”. Scope: fossil preservation of marine and other organisms"
}
